<figure class="access-figure" id="access-definer-model" aria-labelledby="access-definer-caption">
  <figcaption id="access-definer-caption"><span class="access-number">Figure 5</span> Which tenant mapping does the function trust?</figcaption>
  <div class="access-panel">
    <p class="access-kicker">Customer lookup · customer 4 requested · two independent definitions</p>
    <div class="access-identity-pair"><div><span>session_user</span><b>shop_support</b><small>Original database login</small></div><div><span>current_user inside function</span><b>shop_lookup</b><small>Function owner’s privileges</small></div></div>
    <div class="access-map-pair"><div class="access-gate" data-map="trusted"><b>shop_private.support_scope</b><span>shop_support → tenant 10</span><small>Caller cannot change this table</small></div><div class="access-gate" data-map="temp"><b>pg_temp.support_scope</b><span>shop_support → tenant 20</span><small>Counterexample: caller’s own table</small></div></div>
    <p class="access-arrow" data-resolution data-live>↓ enter function</p>
    <div class="access-gate"><b>shop.customers · row 4</b><span>Tenant 20 · Rowan Vale</span><small>shop_lookup has a SELECT policy allowing its lookup</small></div>
    <p class="access-result" data-result data-live>Result pending</p>
    <p class="access-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The caller asks for customer 4. Its login is mapped to tenant 10 in the protected table.</p>
    <label class="access-option">Definition <select data-definition><option value="safe">Qualified objects; fixed search_path</option><option value="unsafe">Unqualified mapping; caller search_path</option></select></label>
    <div class="access-controls" aria-label="Figure 5 playback"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span></div>
    <div class="access-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="access-caption">The function owner can read the needed customer columns; the function must enforce the tenant scope. The unsafe definition resolves an unqualified mapping table through caller-controlled state. The secured definition below names the protected table explicitly and fixes its search path.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><p>Both definitions run as shop_lookup while session_user stays shop_support. The unsafe definition uses an unqualified support_scope name. A caller’s temporary table can map that login to tenant 20, so it returns Rowan. The secure definition joins shop_private.support_scope, where the login maps to tenant 10; customer 4 does not match and no row returns. Setting shop.tenant_id to 20 does not alter that protected mapping.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  const root=document.querySelector('#access-definer-model');
  if(root){
    const select=root.querySelector('[data-definition]');
    const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw(step){
      const safe=select.value==='safe';
      const texts=safe?['The caller asks for customer 4. Its login is mapped to tenant 10 in the protected table.','SECURITY DEFINER changes current_user to shop_lookup. session_user remains shop_support, so the lookup can identify the original login.','The qualified name selects shop_private.support_scope. The caller’s temporary table cannot replace this reference. The protected mapping yields tenant 10.','Customer 4 has tenant 20. It does not join the authorised tenant 10 mapping, so no row returns. The same function returns Mina for customer 1.']:['The same caller has also made a temporary support_scope mapping itself to tenant 20. It has granted shop_lookup permission to read that counterfeit table.','The unsafe function also runs as shop_lookup. Raising authority does not establish which tenant the caller may read.','The unqualified support_scope name resolves to the temporary table first. Its counterfeit mapping yields tenant 20.','The query joins Rowan’s tenant 20 and returns customer 4. This counterexample is why naming and dependency privileges belong in the security boundary.'];
      root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=texts[step];
      root.querySelector('[data-resolution]').textContent=step<2?'↓ enter function':safe?'↓ protected mapping yields 10':'↓ counterfeit mapping yields 20';
      root.querySelector('[data-result]').textContent=step<3?'Result pending':safe?'0 rows · customer 4 is outside tenant 10':'1 row · Rowan Vale disclosed';
      root.querySelectorAll('[data-map]').forEach(el=>el.classList.toggle('access-active',step>=2&&el.dataset.map===(safe?'trusted':'temp')));
    }});
    select.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
  }
</script>
